First fix proposed in the review:

// progress.repository.ts
UPDATE lesson_progress SET percent = GREATEST(percent, $4)
WHERE user_id = $1 AND course_id = $2 AND lesson_id = $3;

// progress.service.ts
await this.progress.raise(userId, courseId, lessonId, percent);
const coursePercent = await this.progress.coursePercent(userId, courseId);
if (coursePercent === 100) await this.certificates.issue(userId, courseId);

API log for one learner:

14:02:10.481 POST /progress/events ev_802 whf-10 100 -> 200 (2.4 s, client timed out)
14:02:12.903 POST /progress/events ev_802 whf-10 100 -> 200 (retry)

Statement: "Because the update uses GREATEST, this code can no longer issue two certificates when the final event is retried."

Second fix, in one transaction per event:

BEGIN;
INSERT INTO processed_events (event_id, received_at) VALUES ($1, now())
  ON CONFLICT (event_id) DO NOTHING
  RETURNING event_id;
-- no row returned: ROLLBACK and answer { status: "duplicate" }
-- one row returned: raise the lesson percent, check for completion, COMMIT

processed_events.event_id is the primary key. The mobile app's offline queue and its retry deliver ev_802 twice, 4 ms apart, to two API instances.

Statement: "Even though both deliveries run at the same time, only one of them gets a row back from the INSERT, so the progress update and the completion check run once for ev_802."
